+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+A positive sub-30 future plan keeps button deceleration, while cancellation waits for a sub-30 current planned speed too. Explicit zero-plan, selected, navigation and close-lead low targets retain their existing conditions. Confirmation remains 0.3s; a low forecast still blocks automatic SET. This is not a measured-vehicle-speed threshold or automatic braking.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Use for Porter II EV with SpeedFromPCM=0. Automatic SET is a separate setting; switching this setting OFF does not itself re-engage cruise.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+Cancellation does not brake or stop the vehicle. TX echo does not prove ECU acceptance; actual stock OFF feedback must be checked.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
 <!-- CARROT:MANUAL:END PorterAutoCancelBelow30 -->
 
